      "en": "SABINE (Scene 33, turn 322): Why are you so bent on lighting that old lantern every evening, Raymond? You know quite well that the passive defense regulations impose total blackout upon us. If the patrols see this glow... We experience thus the significance of vigilant fidelity that maintains the presence of hope at the heart of historical adversity."
